From cbe693a9a81d93c60b484c5a8c98de6892c3db5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:54:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kernels: action and diagonal of the tangent operator without
 assembly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The action of the tangent operator on increments of the unknowns,
Σ Bᵀ K B x w det J, and its diagonal are computed by kernels from the
tangent operator blocks, without assembling it (lot L3):
- batch::computeGradientsIncrements: increments of the gradients, by
  the kernel of the gradients, without the macroscopic gradients nor the
  identity of the deformation gradient;
- batch::multiplyByTangentOperatorBlocks: ds = K dg at each point;
- the kernel of the inner forces adds Bᵀ ds w det J;
- batch::addStiffnessMatricesDiagonals: the kernel of the stiffness
  matrices restricted to the pairs of a node with itself, the diagonals
  being added element by element in the layout of the element
  restriction of MFEM;
- AbstractBehaviourIntegrator::addTangentOperatorActionByKernels and
  addTangentOperatorDiagonalByKernels, implemented by the standard
  behaviour integrators, and the corresponding methods of
  MultiMaterialNonLinearIntegrator on the local vectors of the finite
  element space.

The checks shared by the computations by kernels of the standard
behaviour integrators (integration rule, kind of the gradients,
geometric data) are factored (getKernelsData), as the view of the
tangent operator blocks (readTangentOperatorBlocks).

GradientsKernelsTest compares the action and the diagonal with the
product by the matrix assembled by MFEM and its diagonal.
